Snapdragon Game Super Resolution 1 (SGSR 1)

sgsr1.frag, and the SPIR-V compiled from it in sgsr1_frag_spv.h, are adapted from Qualcomm's SGSR 1
mobile shader:
https://github.com/SnapdragonGameStudios/snapdragon-gsr/blob/d926f074bcb9d714e179f1ce0fcb9ee2eeb5074e/sgsr/v1/include/glsl/sgsr1_shader_mobile.frag
Upstream revision: d926f074bcb9d714e179f1ce0fcb9ee2eeb5074e
Shader sha256: 93e8db987dc79f62e68805f968d63989e5d50daebe4d040e4c7104047ad49139
Shader copyright: Copyright (c) 2025, Qualcomm Innovation Center, Inc. All rights reserved.

The fused YCbCr form follows RubyLight's GPL-3.0 Vulkan port:
https://github.com/RamazanKara/rubylight-android/blob/2293aa2705b42040780b97e4052739be1822043d/app/src/main/jni/pyrowave-renderer/shaders/sgsr.frag
RubyLight revision: 2293aa2705b42040780b97e4052739be1822043d
Port sha256: 2f4d7754d7801fd26ec972683154505f0e79d6b25e8227ab33a7a26b7ff79cf2

Nova's changes are listed at the top of sgsr1.frag: edges on luma, Nova's own colour conversion and
coordinates, fp32, a clamp before and after the delta, a filter whose weights sum to zero or less left
unfiltered, and Qualcomm's default edge sharpness of 2.0, fixed.

